// ESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N16R8. Pin numbers and names are Table 3-1 of the
// ESP32-S3-WROOM-1 & WROOM-1U Datasheet v1.8. Leads 1, 40 and 41 are GND
// (pin 41 is the EPAD). 3V3 joins the chip's VCC, the power inputs of
// Table 2-11, and not VDD_SPI. EN joins CHIP_PU.
// Table 1-1: this ordering is 16 MB quad SPI flash and 8 MB octal SPI PSRAM.
// Note 4: the PSRAM is in the chip package. The features list names a 40 MHz
// crystal. Figure 8-1 labels Y1 40 MHz, ±10 ppm, and does not name its package,
// so no crystal part is placed. The kind models the flash and the PSRAM.
// GPIO26 to GPIO32 stay unwired: Table 3-1 does not bring them out. GPIO33 and
// GPIO34 are not castellations. IO35 to IO37 are pins 28 to 30, and note b says
// they are connected to the octal PSRAM and are not available.
