    { "what": "EN", "pins": ["EN"], "why": "EN is the chip's CHIP_PU, Table 2-1 pin 4 of the ESP32-S3 Series Datasheet v2.2. The esp32s3 kind has no reset pin, so this pin does not reset the model." },
    { "what": "IO35, IO36 and IO37", "pins": ["IO35", "IO36", "IO37"], "why": "Table 3-1 note b: on a module with octal SPI PSRAM, pins IO35, IO36 and IO37 are connected to that PSRAM and are not available for other uses. The kind has no pad for GPIO33 to GPIO37." },
    { "what": "GPIOs the module does not bring out", "why": "Table 3-1 does not bring out GPIO26 to GPIO32, which Figure 8-1 ties to the quad flash, or GPIO33 and GPIO34, which are not castellations. The kind models the 16 MB flash and the in-package PSRAM, so those chip pins have no net." },
    { "what": "crystal, flash and PSRAM", "why": "The features list includes a 40 MHz crystal oscillator. Figure 8-1 labels Y1 40 MHz, ±10 ppm, and says C1 and C4 vary with the crystal. It does not name the crystal package, so none is placed. The kind's clock is that 40 MHz. Table 1-1 gives this ordering 16 MB quad flash and 8 MB octal PSRAM, and note 4 says the PSRAM is in the chip package." }
